 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "pesachim.68b.2",
   "daf": "68b",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "הַרְכָּבָתוֹ וַהֲבָאָתוֹ וְכוּ׳. וּרְמִינְהוּ: חוֹתְכִין יַבֶּלֶת בַּמִּקְדָּשׁ, אֲבָל לֹא בַּמְּדִינָה. וְאִם בִּכְלִי — כָּאן וְכָאן אָסוּר.",
   "en": "The mishna also taught that «carrying» the Paschal lamb through a public domain, «bringing it» from outside the Shabbat limit and cutting off its wart do not override Shabbat. The Gemara «raises a contradiction» from another mishna in tractate Eiruvin, which teaches: «One may cut off a wart» by hand on Shabbat «in the Temple but not in» the rest of «the country» outside the Temple. «And if» the wart is to be removed «with an instrument, it is forbidden» both «here,» in the Temple, «and there,» outside the Temple. From here we see that in the Temple cutting off a wart, at least by hand, is permitted."
  }
 ],
